Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) and Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA ), I have the right to request verification of debts that are alleged to be mine. A vague confirmation of verification is insufficient. Therefore, I am requesting the actual names of the documents used in the verification process and copies of the following : 1. A copy of any original signed contract or application bearing my signature.

2. A detailed billing statement or account statement showing the transactions that led to the debt, including dates and amounts.

3. Any proof of identity used to open or maintain the account, including identification documents, IP address logs, or phone numbers associated with the account.

4. Any investigative report or internal review process you conducted to determine the debt was validly mine.

5. A copy of the fraud investigation file if one was opened upon my report of identity theft. 

As a victim of identity theft, I have a right to be fully informed of the evidence used to associate me with these debts. If you can not provide the above documentation, I request that these accounts be removed from my credit report and all collection efforts cease immediately. 

Please consider this a formal request for verification under federal law. If I do not receive a complete response within 30 days, I will consider further actions including complaints with the FTC, state attorney general, and additional legal counsel. 

