14123932,2025-06-18,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Information belongs to someone else,"XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX Experian P.O. XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX RE : Report Number : XXXX Subject : Formal Dispute and Request for Reinvestigation under FCRA 611 and 605B Re : Reinsertion of Blocked Account XXXX  Acct # XXXX To Whom It May Concern, This letter is in response to your recent notice regarding the re-insertion of previously blocked information related to the above-referenced account, based on allegations of either a material misrepresentation or other disqualifying factor under 15 U.S.C. 1681c-2 ( FCRA 605B ). I hereby dispute the reinsertion of this account and request that you provide the legally required documentation that substantiates your action.

1. Improper Reinsertion Lack of Proper Notification under FCRA 611 ( a ) ( 5 ) ( B ) ( ii ) Under FCRA 611 ( a ) ( 5 ) ( B ) ( ii ), if information is reinserted into a consumers file after being deleted or blocked due to fraud, the consumer reporting agency ( CRA ) must provide written notice to the consumer within five business days of the reinsertion and include : The name of the furnisher, The address and phone number of the furnisher, and A statement that the information was reinserted.

