14245558,2025-06-23,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"This letter serves as a second formal notice regarding fraudulent accounts that remain on my credit file, despite my initial dispute dated XX/XX/year> and supporting documentation that I provided, including my Identity Theft Report ( FTC Complaint # XXXX ). These accounts were identified as the result of identity theft : Creditor : XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX Account Number : XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Under 15 U.S.C. 1681c-2 ( FCRA Section 605B ), you were legally required to block and remove these fraudulent accounts from my credit report within four ( 4 ) business days of receiving my valid identity theft documentation. The failure to do so constitutes a violation of federal law.

Applicable Legal Requirements : 15 U.S.C. 1681c-2 ( a ) : Upon receiving appropriate proof of identity, a copy of an identity theft report, and a specific request, a credit reporting agency must block the reporting of information resulting from identity theft within 4 business days.

15 U.S.C. 1681c-2 ( c ) : A CRA may not refuse to block fraudulent information except under narrowly defined circumstances ( e.g., material misrepresentation or fraud by the consumer, neither of which applies in my case ).

15 U.S.C. 1681i ( a ) : A CRA must conduct a reasonable reinvestigation and delete unverifiable or inaccurate information within 30 days of a dispute.

15 U.S.C. 1681e ( b ) : You are required to follow reasonable procedures to assure maximum possible accuracy of the information in consumer reports. Continuing to report fraudulent accounts after receiving identity theft documentation fails to meet this standard.

Final Demand : I hereby demand : 1. Immediate deletion and blocking of the above-listed fraudulent accounts from my credit file.

2. A written statement confirming deletion and blocking of these accounts.

3. An updated credit report reflecting these changes.

4. Confirmation that notices of correction have been sent to any entity that received my report within the past six months, as required by 15 U.S.C. 1681i ( d ).

If I do not receive confirmation within 10 business days, I will file additional complaints with the CFPB, FTC, State Attorney Generals Office, and consider legal action under 15 U.S.C. 1681n ( willful noncompliance ) and 1681o ( negligent noncompliance ), seeking damages as provided by law.",,"EQUIFAX, INC.",VA,22193,,Web,2025-06-23,Closed with explanation,Yes
