14341721,2025-06-27,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"XX/XX/XXXX Reporting on Account # XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Demand for Permanent Deletion and Compensation Dear XXXX, Experian, and XXXX, Pursuant to the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), 15 U.S.C. 1681i ( a ), and Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA ), 15 U.S.C. 1692, I am submitting this formal dispute regarding inaccurate, unverifiable, and misleading information reported on my credit file for the account listed below. This letter is structured in the Automated Credit Dispute Verification ( ACDV ) format, as required under the e-OSCAR system, and demands a thorough investigation, correction, or permanent deletion of the disputed items. I also request compensation for damages caused by these inaccuracies, as permitted under 15 U.S.C. 1681n and 1681o.

Account Information * Account Number : XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Account Type : Installment ( Unsecured Loan ) * Account Status : Transferred * Date Opened : XX/XX/XXXX ( Experian/XXXX  ) / XX/XX/XXXX ( XXXX  ) XXXX Balance : {$0.00} * Payment Status : * XXXX  : Late 60 Days * Experian : Late 30 Days * XXXX : Late 60 Days * Last Reported : XX/XX/XXXX ( XXXX  )/ XX/XX/XXXX ( XXXX ) XXXX Comments : Transferred to another lender or claim purchased; Sold to : XXXX * Date of Last Payment : XX/XX/XXXX ( XXXX  )/ XX/XX/XXXX ( XXXX/Experian ) * Date of Last Active : XX/XX/XXXX ( Experian )/ XX/XX/XXXX ( XXXX  )/ XX/XX/XXXX ( XXXX  ) Dispute Details and Violations The information reported on this account contains multiple inaccuracies and violates several provisions of the FCRA, FDCPA, Metro 2 , and XXXX  standards . Below, I outline each issue and the applicable laws : 1. Inaccurate Payment Status Reporting * Issue : The account is reported as Late 60 Days ( XXXX ) and Late 30 Days ( Experian ), despite the account being transferred with a {$0.00} balance. This is inconsistent and misleading, as a transferred account with no balance should not reflect delinquency.

